{"title":"Asymptote (Vector Graphics Language)","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"border:1px solid black; background:#CEE0F2;text-align:center;\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#B0C4DE;\"><b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Asymptote (Vector Graphics Language)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Asymptote:_Getting_Started\" title=\"Asymptote: Getting Started\">Getting&#160;Started</a> - <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Asymptote:_Basics\" title=\"Asymptote: Basics\">Basics</a> - <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Asymptote:_Drawing\" title=\"Asymptote: Drawing\">Drawing</a> - <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Asymptote:_Labeling\" title=\"Asymptote: Labeling\"> Labeling</a> - <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Asymptote:_Filling\" title=\"Asymptote: Filling\"> Filling</a> - <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Asymptote:_Useful_functions\" title=\"Asymptote: Useful functions\">Useful functions</a> - <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Asymptote:_Useful_commands_and_their_Output\" title=\"Asymptote: Useful commands and their Output\">Examples</a> - <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Asymptote:_Macros_and_Packages\" title=\"Asymptote: Macros and Packages\">Macros&#160;and&#160;Packages</a><br />\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Asymptote:_Help\" title=\"Asymptote: Help\">Help</a> - <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Asymptote:_Reference\" title=\"Asymptote: Reference\">Reference</a> - <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Asymptote:_Advanced\" title=\"Asymptote: Advanced\"> Advanced&#160;Asymptote</a> - <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=3D_graphics_for_Asymptote\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"3D graphics for Asymptote\">3D Graphics</a> - <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Asymptote:_CSE5\" title=\"Asymptote: CSE5\">CSE5 Package</a> - <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Asymptote:_How_to\" title=\"Asymptote: How to\">How to</a>\n</p>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><b>Asymptote</b> is a powerful vector graphics language designed for creating mathematical diagrams and figures.  It can output images in either eps or pdf format, and is compatible with the standard mathematics typesetting language, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=LaTeX\" title=\"LaTeX\">LaTeX</a>.  It is also a complete programming language, and has cleaner syntax than its predecessor, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://netlib.bell-labs.com/who/hobby/MetaPost.html\">MetaPost</a>, which was a language used only for two-dimensional graphics.\n</p><p>You can start with this <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ruAiHB05hoY\">AoPS Asymptote Quick Start Video</a>.\n</p><p>Here is an example of an image that can be produced using Asymptote:\n</p>\n<center><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Figure1.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/8/8e/Figure1.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"143\" height=\"133\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span></center>\n<p>In a sense, Asymptote is the ruler and compass of typesetting.\n</p><p><br />\nYou can use Asymptote on the AoPSWiki right now, by enclosing the Asymptote code within <tt>&lt;asy&gt;...&lt;/asy&gt;</tt> tags. For example, the following code\n</p>\n<pre>&lt;asy&gt;\ndraw((0,0)--(3,7),red);\ndot((0,0));\ndot((3,7));\ndot((7,6));\ndot((7,7));\ndot((6,7));\ndot((3,0));\ndot((9,7));\ndot((8,4));\ndot((3,8));\nlabel(\"Produced with Asymptote \"+version.VERSION,point(S),2S);\n&lt;/asy&gt;</pre>\n<p>created the picture \n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/8/d88f3bbba665110715eb36189c8dc425965c3be9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(3,7),red); dot((0,0)); dot((3,7)); label(&quot;Produced with Asymptote &quot;+version.VERSION,point(S),2S); [/asy]\" width=\"272\" height=\"252\" /></center>\n<p>And on the AoPS forums you can use <tt>[asy]..[/asy]</tt>\n</p>\n<pre>[asy]\ndraw((0,0)--(3,7),red);\ndot((0,0));\ndot((3,7));\nlabel(\"Produced with Asymptote \"+version.VERSION,point(S),2S);\n[/asy]</pre>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/7/b57775c768cabba6a2ac4465219858d7f0636b41.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A,B,C,X,Y,Z; A = (0,0); B = (1,0); C = (0.3,0.8); draw(A--B--C--A); X = (B+C)/2; Y = (A+C)/2; Z = (A+B)/2; draw(A--X, red); draw(B--Y,red); draw(C--Z,red);[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"202\" />\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017214005\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.031 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.082 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 22/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 793/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1004/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.295      1 Template:Asymptote\n100.00%   14.295      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4452:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017214005 and revision id 273079. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}